,uint256,uint256) pure returns (uint256)"}},"id":8382,"isConstant":false,"isLValue":false,"isPure":false,"kind":"functionCall","lValueRequested":false,"nameLocations":[],"names":[],"nodeType":"FunctionCall","src":"29151:87:14","tryCall":false,"typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}},"src":"29136:102:14","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}},"src":"29126:112:14","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}},"id":8385,"nodeType":"ExpressionStatement","src":"29126:112:14"}]},"documentation":{"id":8202,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"27190:856:14","text":" @notice Previews `withdrawPair(shares)` to the wei: what burning `shares` would pay right now.\n @dev Same arithmetic as `withdrawPair`, from StateView reads, balances and the factory's fee only: for every\n      non-empty band the principal of `floor(L * shares / supply)` at the current price, rounded down exactly as\n      Uniswap pays a removal, plus `floor(shares * (idle + F - protocolFee) / supply)`. Called directly on the\n      module (`VaultM5Module(vault.m5Module())`), never through delegatecall, and changes nothing. Reverts with\n      `ZeroValue` for zero shares or more shares than exist.\n @param vault Vault to preview.\n @param shares Shares that would be burned.\n @return amount0 Currency0 the withdrawal would pay.\n @return amount1 Currency1 the withdrawal would pay."},"functionSelector":"6114be43","id":8387,"implemented":true,"kind":"function","modifiers":[],"name":"previewWithdrawPair","nameLocation":"28060:19:14","nodeType":"FunctionDefinition","parameters":{"id":8208,"nodeType":"ParameterList","parameters":[{"constant":false,"id":8205,"mutability":"mutable","name":"vault","nameLocation":"28087:5:14","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":8387,"src":"28080:12:14","stateVariable":false,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_contract$_IVault_$11047","typeString":"c